{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And moreover she is indeed.</b> אמנה in my mouth, <b>my sister, my father's daughter, is she</b> — yet she was not literally his father's daughter, but the daughter of Haran, who was the son of Terah, as it is said (Genesis 11:29–30): בת הרן אבי מלכה ואבי יסכה — 'the daughter of Haran, the father of Milcah and the father of Iscah'; and יסכה, that is Sarai; and the sons of sons — they are as sons; and from this he said בת אבי, that is, the daughter of my father's son."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:13:47.921337002Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}